{"id":"DRKS00038045","src":"drks","title":"Evaluation of Clinical Management and Outcome in High-Risk or Recurrent Endometrial Cancer","official":"","summary":"Die Identifizierung von Risikogruppen durch molekulargenetische Testung und die Einführung neuer Behandlungsmöglichkeiten z.B. durch Immuntherapien haben erhebliche Auswirkungen auf die Behandlungsstrategien in allen Tumorstadien des Endometriumkarzinoms. Die Daten aus der Praxis zur Wirksamkeit und Sicherheit von Immuntherapien sind nach wie vor begrenzt. Darüber hinaus ist die Umsetzung dieser neuen wissenschaftlichen Ergebnisse und Empfehlungen in die klinische Praxis noch nicht gut bekannt. Eine umfassende Analyse solcher Fälle könnte dazu beitragen, Wissenslücken zu schließen und zukünftige klinische Entscheidungen zu unterstützen.\r\nDiese retrospektive, multizentrische Studie dient der Erhebung von Daten zu den Ausgangsmerkmalen, Behandlungsstrategien sowie klinischen Ergebnissen aller Patientinnen, bei denen zwischen 2023 und 2025 in gynäkologischen Krebszentren der AGO-Studiengruppe ein Hochrisiko- oder rezidivierender Endometriumkarzinom diagnostiziert wurde.","conditions":["Malignant neoplasm: Endometrium"],"interventions":[{"type":"ARM","name":"The routine treatment and clinical outcomes of patients diagnosed with high-risk or recurrent endometrial cancer between 2023 and 2025 in gynecological cancer centers of the AGO study group will be recorded."}],"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\nPrimarily high-risk or recurrent endometrial cancer \r\n- High-risk is defined according to ESGO guidelines 2025, integrating FIGO 2023 into molecular subtyping (Concin N. Lancet Oncol et al. 2025) or\r\n- According to FIGO 2009 \r\nAll stages and all histologies with p53 (with p53 aberrant tumor biology and myometrial invasion.\r\nAll stages with serous od undifferentiated carcinoma including carcinosarcoma with myometrial invasion\r\nAll stage III or IV at first diagnosis (regardless of residual tumor, histology and molecular subtype) or \r\n- recurrent endometrial cancer\r\n- Treatment in participating centers between 07/2023 and 07/2025\nExclusion criteria:\nTrue sarkomas","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"FEMALE","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":null,"start":"2026-01-27","pcd":"2026-10-31","upd":"2026-09-16","sponsor":"AGO Research GmbH, AGO Studiengruppe","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Prof. Dr. med. Lars Hanker · Klinik für Frauenheilkunde und Geburtshilfe Universitätsklinikum Münster (UKM) · 49 251 83-48201 · lars.hanker@ukmuenster.de"],"sites":[{"f":"Klinik für Frauenheilkunde und Geburtshilfe Universitätsklinikum Münster (UKM)","city":"Münster","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":51.9624,"lon":7.6257},{"f":"Klinik für Gynäkologie & Gynäkologische Onkologie, KEM | Evang. Kliniken Essen-Mitte","city":"Essen","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":51.4566,"lon":7.0123},{"f":"Klinik und Poliklinik für Frauenheilkunde und Geburtshilfe,  LMU Klinikum","city":"München","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":51.607,"lon":13.3124},{"f":"Universitätsklinikum Köln","city":"Köln","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":50.9384,"lon":6.96},{"f":"Universitäts-Frauenklinik","city":"Heidelberg","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":49.4077,"lon":8.6908},{"f":"Caritas-Krankenhaus St. Josef","city":"Regensburg","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":49.0151,"lon":12.1016},{"f":"Universitätsmedizin Greifswald - Universitätsfrauenklinik","city":"Greifswald","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":54.0891,"lon":13.4024},{"f":"Frauenklinik des Universitätsklinikums Tübingen","city":"Tübingen","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":48.5227,"lon":9.0522},{"f":"Universitätsklinikum der TU","city":"Dresden","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":51.0509,"lon":13.7383},{"f":"Universitätsklinikum Schleswig-Holstein - Campus Lübeck","city":"Lübeck","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":53.8689,"lon":10.6873},{"f":"Klinikum Südstadt Rostock","city":"Rostock","zi